WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.840
What we've been working
on for the past year

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.020
almost year is just kind

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.447
of the training method that I do.

00:00:12.447 --> 00:00:15.792
And it's the same training
method that I use for Kim.

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:18.800
It's mostly about eating.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.775
I mean, people think it's in the exercise,

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:23.920
but if you're not eating
right consistently,

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:26.234
then it's just never going to happen.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:30.761
You know, her diet has come a long way

00:00:30.761 --> 00:00:33.355
and has changed a lot in terms of

00:00:33.355 --> 00:00:36.720
just eliminating processed
foods and just getting

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.120
her to eat real food.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.382
So if it comes in a box,

00:00:39.382 --> 00:00:42.114
if it didn't grow off a tree or

00:00:42.114 --> 00:00:44.494
the earth didn't give it to you,

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:46.960
then just stay away from it.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.940
Fresh foods, unprocessed
foods and only water.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.640
As for the work outs,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.277
I would do something that's mixed,

00:00:57.277 --> 00:00:59.140
so that there's weight training,

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.196
there's high intensity interval training

00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:03.722
and there's steady state cardio.

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:05.940
For now, you know I train Kim

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.840
consistently. Sometimes I train

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.420
her sisters Khloe and Kourtney.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.930
Kim: She's even Snapchatting
in my workout with Melissa.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.210
I give her the privilege of working out

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.928
with her one time.

00:01:16.928 --> 00:01:19.990
I honestly, I just love her.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.430
She's also like one of the best clients

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:23.584
that you could ever have.

00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:26.520
She doesn't cancel. She's always there.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.070
- [Kim] This is what I'm doing today.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.650
A lot of our sessions are at 6 a.m.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:31.920
I wake up at 4.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.660
So we train about five, six days a week.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.080
It ranges from an hour
to an hour and a half.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.080
We do a lot of squats,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.220
dead lifts, chest press,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.400
overhead press,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.320
a ton of sprints.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.980
We do pull-ups, dips,

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.820
but I would

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.560
say that 85% of our
training is weight training.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.520
You have to put the work in.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.580
You have to be intense,

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:12.660
you have to struggle with
every rep and feel it.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.320
It doesn't mean that

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.680
you're gonna be Arnold and get huge.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.980
- [Kim] Hey guys, she's trying to kill me.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.020
- Only a little bit.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.300
- [Kim] Officially trying to kill me.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.500
- In the beginning, I
was sitting on my couch.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.660
I had gained 70 pounds with my daughter

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.460
and I saw this infomercial

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.820
for Insanity, which is
a home workout program.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.960
And I saw these people's transformations.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.540
And I packed up all my food,

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.460
I never cheated, only drank water,

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.760
never missed a workout

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.980
and 60 days later I was 40 pounds lighter.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.420
I decided I wanted to do
a bodybuilding competition

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.280
in December of 2015. I won first place

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.060
in Miss Figure and Miss
Physique and that's

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.520
when Kim contacted me.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.980
So she saw my transformation
picture on Instagram.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.960
She was scrolling through
Instagram at 4 o'clock

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.940
in the morning and she was
like, "Wow, this woman,

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.900
she's a Mom. She lives
like a regular life.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.040
Look at how she changed her life."

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.980
She was looking for something
that was sustainable.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:14.620
She didn't want to just
lose weight fast and then

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.220
you know gain it again. It's a lifestyle.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:21.100
I had no expectations of
becoming a celebrity trainer.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.120
I'm not thinking, "Oh yeah,

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.700
I'm gonna train Oprah tomorrow."

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.920
I just hope that they

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.460
get the results they're looking for.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:34.460
And every time she sees
a new muscle growing

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.220
or new lines, new definition -

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.680
- [KIm] Do you guys see my muscles?

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.040
- The look on her face

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.660
just makes me like

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.460
super excited for her,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.720
because I know exactly
what that feels like.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.380
- Hamstrings, my favorite.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.240
- Yeah, except that you're doing it

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.040
with that bar.
- Oh, she has the light bar.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.000
This is what I'm doing.
- Exactly.

